WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:09.500
<v Briefing>Plumbers miss up to forty percent of their calls, and eighty-five percent of those callers never call back. That's thirteen thousand dollars a month, gone.

2
00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:18.852
<v Agent>Hi Maria, Sam from Blue Ridge Plumbing — sorry we missed you, the crew was under a sink. What's going on?

3
00:00:18.902 --> 00:00:22.430
<v Caller>My kitchen sink is completely backed up, nothing's draining.

4
00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:28.096
<v Agent>We can be there today, two to four — the $89 dispatch fee goes toward the repair. Book it?

5
00:00:28.146 --> 00:00:28.818
<v Caller>Yes, please.

6
00:00:28.868 --> 00:00:33.044
<v Agent>Booked. You'll get a text with the plumber's name and a tracking link.

7
00:00:33.494 --> 00:00:40.190
<v Briefing>Missed call, texted in eight seconds, called back in fifty-two, booked. Three hundred and twenty dollars recovered.

8
00:00:39.794 --> 00:00:44.954
<v Briefing>And the estimates nobody chased? The agent follows up, handles the objection, and closes.

9
00:00:42.794 --> 00:00:48.530
<v Agent>Hi Tom, Sam from Blue Ridge — checking in on the water heater estimate we sent Monday. Any questions?

10
00:00:48.580 --> 00:00:52.540
<v Caller>Honestly it's the price. Twenty-four hundred — we were going to wait.

11
00:00:52.590 --> 00:00:59.166
<v Agent>Fair. We can do zero percent for twelve months — two hundred a month — and install Thursday morning. Hold Thursday?

12
00:00:59.216 --> 00:01:00.584
<v Caller>Yeah… let's do Thursday.

13
00:01:06.934 --> 00:01:10.822
<v Briefing>Want your missed calls and unsold estimates recovered? Let's build it.

